From: rosy-port <ace@localhost>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 14:20:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] 1025 rosy: SpringBoard's screens from the GPU pool too

boot43 (60 Hz panel) made the motion continuous but left a large touch-to-pixel
latency.  The log names the cause:

  SWEET SURF: SpringBoard create id 0 1125x2436 ... -> 0xe00002bd     (65 of 65)
  SWEET SURF: CollectionsPoster create ... -> 0xe00002bd             (15 of 15)
  vm_page_find_contiguous(num=2744,low=0): found 0 pages ...
      scanned 178950 pages... zone_gc called...

2744 pages is exactly 1125x2436x4.  SpringBoard draws its own UI into its
screen-sized surfaces (the window server only composites them), but patch 0989
gave the vince GPU pool to backboardd alone, so every SpringBoard screen fell
through to the scanout path, which needs s->allocSize physically contiguous
below 4 GiB.  It could not find it, the plain wired allocation failed after it,
and the create returned NoMemory -- after an allocation attempt that scanned all
of RAM and ran zone_gc.  That is the latency: not a slow renderer but a full
memory scan per surface create, repeated for every retry.

Give SpringBoard the pool memory the window server's own screens come from, and
raise the pool's screen cap from 8 to 16 so the window server cannot fill it
alone.  topaz tried the same and reverted it (applications' screen-sized
surfaces came out black); on vince the pool surfaces are drawn in place with
vincecache=1 doing the cache maintenance, which is the difference.

Marker for CI: the pool log line now carries the process name.

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetSurface.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetSurface.cpp
index 7190db0..31fa8e8 100644
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetSurface.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetSurface.cpp
@@ -1113,7 +1113,15 @@ IOSurfaceRootUserClient::create(IOExternalMethodArguments *args)
 		char who[32];
 
 		proc_selfname(who, sizeof(who));
-		if (strcmp(who, "backboardd") == 0) {
+		/*
+		 * rosy 1008: SpringBoard as well as the window server. SpringBoard draws its own UI
+		 * into its screen-sized surfaces (the window server only composites them), and with
+		 * the pool closed to it every 1125x2436 create failed: the scanout path had to find
+		 * s->allocSize physically contiguous below 4 GiB, could not, and the plain wired
+		 * allocation failed after it. Each attempt scanned all of RAM and called zone_gc --
+		 * that is the touch-to-pixel latency, not a slow renderer.
+		 */
+		if (strcmp(who, "backboardd") == 0 || strcmp(who, "SpringBoard") == 0) {
 			/* the GPU writes whole tiles: 64 rows past the picture have pages behind them (as for the topaz pool) */
 			uint64_t take = round_page_64(s->allocSize + 64ull * s->bytesPerRow);
 			uint64_t pa = vince_pool_alloc(take);
@@ -1136,8 +1144,8 @@ IOSurfaceRootUserClient::create(IOExternalMethodArguments *args)
 				} else {
 					static uint32_t told;
 					if (told++ < 16) {
-						IOLog("SWEET SURF: surface %ux%u (%llu bytes) in the GPU's pool at %#llx\n", s->width, s->height,
-						    (unsigned long long)take, (unsigned long long)pa);
+						IOLog("SWEET SURF: surface %ux%u (%llu bytes) in the GPU's pool at %#llx (%s)\n", s->width, s->height,
+						    (unsigned long long)take, (unsigned long long)pa, who);
 					}
 				}
 			} else if (pa != 0) {
diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/VinceGPU.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/VinceGPU.cpp
index 136acd9..1acb400 100644
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/VinceGPU.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/VinceGPU.cpp
@@ -529,8 +529,12 @@ vince_pool_alloc(uint64_t size)
 		return 0;
 	}
 	IOLockLock(gPoolLock);
-	/* the buffers of the library need room too: the screens take at most 8 of the pool's 11 MiB pieces */
-	if (gPlaceHeld < 8) {
+	/*
+	 * The buffers of the library need room too: a screen takes ~11.5 MiB of the pool's 192 MiB,
+	 * so 16 of them still leave ~8 MiB for those. rosy 1008: was 8, which the window server
+	 * alone could fill, so SpringBoard's screens were always refused.
+	 */
+	if (gPlaceHeld < 16) {
 		pa = poolAllocLocked(size, true);
 		if (pa != 0) {
 			gPlaceHeld++;
